@startuml
title send / sendkeep / closekeep — best effort
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox
actor "Shell user" as user
participant "CLI\n(short-lived)" as cli
participant "Pi Rust worker\n(session owner)" as worker
participant "Native peer now\nforeground phone in G2.3" as peer
group send: fresh, one-shot session
user -> cli : send "Hello, world!"
cli -> worker : Restricted local socket request
alt Kept session exists
worker --> cli : Busy; retained state unchanged
else No session exists
worker <-> peer : Connect + authenticated handshake (30 s from advertising)
worker -> peer : One encrypted record, fragmented once
peer --> worker : Normal ATT confirmations only
worker -> worker : Disconnect; discard keys/counters
worker --> cli : transport_success=true delivery=unconfirmed
end
end
group sendkeep: worker survives successful CLI exit
user -> cli : sendkeep "Hello, world!"
cli -> worker : Restricted local socket request
alt No session exists
worker <-> peer : Fresh authenticated handshake
worker -> worker : Start 120 s absolute lifetime
else Existing session
worker -> worker : Reserve next sequence/nonce; expiry unchanged
end
worker -> peer : One encrypted record, fragmented once
peer --> worker : Normal ATT confirmations only
worker --> cli : Local result handoff; delivery=unconfirmed
note over worker, peer
No application ACK, receipt, retry or reconnect.
Only the worker retains the live connection and secrets.
end note
end
group closekeep or expiry
user -> cli : closekeep
cli -> worker : Close (absent worker/session: successful no-op)
worker -> peer : One authenticated close if reachable (2 s max)
worker -> worker : Always tear down locally; discard secrets
worker --> cli : local_closed=true remote_close=unconfirmed
note over worker, peer
Expiry cancels active work and destroys keys at 120 s.
Cleanup is bounded to 2 s; close cannot extend lifetime.
Link/subscription loss or failure requires fresh establishment next time.
end note
end
@enduml
